cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DYNAMOS in research, teaching, practice, or derived work, please cite the model."
title: "DYNAMOS: Dynamic Neuro-Operational Systems Model"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Berkling"
    given-names: "Kay"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: 2026-09-26
license: "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22977734
abstract: >-
  DYNAMOS (Dynamic Neuro-Operational Systems Model) is an open, non-diagnostic
  systems-architecture framework for describing how human cognitive-behavioral
  systems operate under meaning, load, interaction, context, and time.
  Version 2.0.0 includes 26 dimensions, 32 PRECEPTA patterns across five domains,
  a browser-based self-reflection instrument, and an experimental participant-
  feedback research loop. The questionnaire and PRECEPTA derivation remain
  explicitly pilot-stage and are not validated diagnostic or psychometric tools.
keywords:
  - neurodiversity
  - dynamic systems
  - cognitive diversity
  - systems architecture
  - knowledge work
  - PRECEPTA
